  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Unsettled weather will persist through the rest of\nthis week and into upcoming weekend with daily chances of \nshowers and thunderstorms with marginal risks of excessive \nrainfall for all or portions of the area.\n\nAs the previous upper cutoff low has dampened into the large\nscale flow aloft the area will remain between the Bermuda high\noff to the east and a upper longwave trough to the west. This\nsetup allows for an ongoing south to southwesterly fetch\nmaintaining ample deep layer moisture advecting northward. With\nno sign of any main feature or wave traversing across the area,\nthe forcing mechanism for convection will largely be daytime\nheating and orographic lift keeping the greatest chances across\nthe mountains each day through the rest of the work week. High\nPWATs in the 1.5 to 2.0 inch range will support hydrometeor\nloading within showers and storms to be efficient rain producers\nand allow for isolated flash flooding potential as well. See the\nhydrology section below for more details.\n\nA weak shortwave along more zonal flow is progged to approach \nthe area Saturday into Saturday night that may focus more \nwidespread or organized convection, otherwise chances for\nshowers and storms decrease some for Sunday into next week\nthough development is still possible mainly in the mountains.",
